{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · why the plane is special","loop":56,"ease":"inout","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[{"t":0,"box":[-0.799826087,-0.109155652,-0.444,0.016173913]},{"t":0.16,"box":[-0.799826087,-0.109155652,-0.444,0.016173913]},{"t":0.19,"box":[-0.42813913,-0.0550956522,-0.182295652,0.0707478261]},{"t":0.33,"box":[-0.42813913,-0.0550956522,-0.182295652,0.0707478261]},{"t":0.36,"box":[-0.16226087,-0.0448695652,-0.0307826087,0.0553043478]},{"t":0.5,"box":[-0.16226087,-0.0448695652,-0.0307826087,0.0553043478]},{"t":0.53,"box":[-0.0273704348,-0.045453913,0.178447826,0.061106087]},{"t":0.67,"box":[-0.0273704348,-0.045453913,0.178447826,0.061106087]},{"t":0.7,"box":[0.207391304,-0.0586956522,0.340434783,0.0743478261]},{"t":0.84,"box":[0.207391304,-0.0586956522,0.340434783,0.0743478261]},{"t":0.87,"box":[0.38013913,-0.0502956522,0.731165217,0.063746087]}],"stops":[0.16,0.33,0.5,0.67,0.84],"beats":[{"title":"One law, from a standpoint","text":"A reader stands at [z = m + iγ](#lit:1) above a line and turns evenly. [Equal turns](#lit:2) land [unevenly](#lit:3), crowding at the foot: the [Cauchy](#lit:4), foot m, height γ.\n\n[Walkers](#lit:5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12) let go at z, wandering until they touch the line, [land by the same law](#lit:13). A new zero and a new thumb carry z, and the law goes with it."},{"title":"Four parts, one law","text":"In the plane the law does four jobs. Put a [reader](#lit:15) inside a circle, off its centre. Its even turn [lands unevenly](#lit:16,17): [L](#lit:21), against the [uniform](#lit:20).\n\n[Twice L less the uniform](#lit:22) is the circle's [harmonic measure](#lit:19), where a walker from the same place lands. Its [mean is the standpoint](#lit:23); the turn's own landings average [half way there](#lit:24). Möbius maps, walkers, powers of one point, the two sweeps' rates: one curve."},{"title":"On the sphere, three","text":"Do the same in a ball, the reader half way out. In the plane the three rules give [one curve](#lit:27). On the sphere they part: [harmonic measure](#lit:28) peaks at 6 times the uniform, [twice the landing less the uniform](#lit:29) at 7, the [Möbius image of the uniform](#lit:30) at 9.\n\nNo choice of its concentration brings the Möbius law within 5% of the walker's. Liouville: in space the only angle-keeping maps are Möbius maps, and they no longer keep heat as heat."},{"title":"Turns that do not take turns","text":"In the plane a turn by α then β ends where β then α does, so turns add. Give [one book](#lit:31,32) a quarter turn about the upright and then about the line toward you, and [another](#lit:33,34) the same two in the other order.\n\nThey end [120° apart](#lit:31,33). Hamilton's quaternions keep division and give up the order; past two dimensions nothing keeps both."},{"title":"The leftover","text":"Carry an [arrow](#lit:41) round a [loop on a sphere](#lit:39,38), as straight as the surface allows: down from the pole, a quarter along the equator, and back up. It comes home [turned 90°](#lit:41) from [where it began](#lit:40), the loop's solid angle, π/2.\n\nIn the plane a loop leaves nothing over. Small turns α and β and both back leave about α·β; physics meets it as Berry's phase, a quantity of directions alone."},{"title":"What survives","text":"The boundary decides it, not the dimension. From a height above a flat wall, in space, the turn and the walker land alike: [one curve](#lit:43,45). Inside a ball, from half way out, they part: within [45°](#lit:47) straight ahead [the walker lands 0.482](#lit:48) of the time, [the turn 0.359](#lit:49).\n\nFrom home, the split, the [corners](#lit:52,51) and the [near field's third](#lit:50) need only the exchange of two shares, and hold in any number of dimensions. [The essay](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/13-why-the-plane-is-special.md)"}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.247826087,0.247826087,-0.247826087,-0.247826087],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":0},{"morph":4},{"morph":13},{"morph":5},{"morph":6},{"morph":7},{"morph":8},{"morph":9},{"morph":10},{"morph":11},{"morph":12},{"morph":2},{"morph":3},{"morph":1},{"morph":14},{"morph":16},{"morph":17},{"morph":18},{"morph":20},{"morph":19},{"morph":21},{"morph":22},{"morph":23},{"morph":15},{"morph":24},{"morph":25},{"morph":26},{"morph":27},{"morph":28},{"morph":29},{"morph":30},{"morph":31},{"morph":32},{"morph":33},{"morph":34},{"morph":35},{"morph":55},{"morph":56},{"morph":57},{"morph":36},{"morph":37},{"morph":38},{"morph":39},{"morph":40},{"morph":41},{"morph":42},{"morph":58},{"morph":59},{"morph":44},{"morph":43},{"morph":45},{"morph":46},{"morph":47},{"morph":48},{"morph":49},{"morph":50},{"morph":51},{"morph":52},{"morph":53},{"morph":54},{"morph":60},{"morph":61}],"morphs":[{"exact":true,"open":true,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.765391304,-0.478434783],"y":[-0.0182608696,-0.0182608696],"r":[0,0],"c":[null,null]}],"fill":null,"inPlace":true,"lag":0,"fx":null,"own":{"parent":-1,"parentAt":null,"follow":null,"look":-1,"lookRef":0,"phase":0,"rate":1,"spin":0,"motion":null,"onto":null,"laps":1,"start":null,"times":null,"clip":{"start":0.004,"len":0.986,"show":"","in":{"kind":"draw","len":0.012}},"eases":null,"straight":false,"trail":null,"cols":null,"path":null},"stroke":"#3b4256","width":2,"strokeOpacity":1},{"exact":true,"open":false,"holes":null,"keys":[{"x":[-0.63783913,-0.640421739,-0.640421739,-0.63783913],"y":[0.00914347826,0.00914347826,0.011726087,0.011726087],"r":[0,0,0,0],"c":[[-0.638551304,0.00843130435,-0.639709565,0.00843130435],[-0.641133913,0.00985565217,-0.641133913,0.011013913],[-0.639709565,0.0124382609,-0.638551304,0.0124382609],[-0.637126957,0.011013913,-0.637126957,0.00985565217]]},{"x":[-0.63783913,-0.640421739,-0.640421739,-0.63783913],"y":[0.00914347826,0.00914347826,0.011726087,0.011726087],"r":[0,0,0,0],